// Facade: process filter_openssh_journal
// Test corpus: synthetic (pam_unix / sshd sample bodies referenced
//              in this header's drop/pass tables)
//
// systemd-journald groups log lines by `_SYSTEMD_UNIT`, so subscribing
// to `_SYSTEMD_UNIT=ssh.service` collects every line emitted by the
// sshd process — which includes lines from PAM modules and other
// stacks invoked from inside sshd. Those lines are NOT sshd protocol
// vocabulary; feeding them straight into [`parse_openssh`](../parsers/parse_openssh.limpid)
// would land them in its error route on every login.
//
// Run this ahead of `parse_openssh` only when the upstream input is
// journald (or anything else that aggregates by Unix process /
// cgroup); for native syslog feeds (where each daemon has its own
// syslogtag) this filter is a no-op and can be omitted.
//
// Usage (filter sits between parse_journald and the openssh bridge):
//
//   def pipeline ssh {
//       input ssh_in
//       process parse_journald | filter_openssh_journal | {
//           workspace.openssh = {
//               body:     workspace.journald.MESSAGE,
//               pid:      coalesce(workspace.journald._PID,
//                                  workspace.journald.SYSLOG_PID),
//               hostname: workspace.journald._HOSTNAME,
//               time:     to_int(workspace.journald.__REALTIME_TIMESTAMP) * 1000
//           }
//       } | parse_openssh | compose_ocsf | ocsf_to_egress
//       output sink
//   }
//
// Filter scope (drops; keep growing this list as new noise sources
// surface):
//
//   - `pam_unix(sshd:auth|session|account|password): ...`
//     PAM stack lifecycle events. The matching sshd-side messages
//     (`Accepted`, `Failed`, `Disconnected`) carry the same
//     authentication outcome with richer fields, so the PAM lines are
//     redundant for OCSF Authentication purposes.
//
// What is NOT filtered — anything starting with sshd's own vocabulary
// (`Accepted`, `Failed`, `Invalid user`, `Disconnected`, `Connection
// closed by`, `Connection reset by`, `Did not receive identification
// string`, …). Those flow through unchanged for `parse_openssh` to
// classify.

// Process: filter_openssh_journal
// Summary: Strip PAM-stack noise from a journal-sourced sshd stream ahead of parse_openssh.
// Reads: workspace.journald.* (from parse_journald)
//        .MESSAGE (required, String) — sshd body candidate
// Writes: ingress
def process filter_openssh_journal {
    let body = coalesce(workspace.journald.MESSAGE, "")
    if regex_match(body, "^pam_unix\\(sshd:[a-z]+\\):") {
        drop
    }
}
